# Reference checkouts: fetched, pinned by the ledger in .agents/TOOLS.md, never edited.
references/

# The Bend launcher: a two-line shim over references/bend.
/bin/bend

# Native output from `bend x.bend -o x`, and the GPU program beside it.
*.bin
*.gpu

# Python scratch from the oracle harness. The tinygrad/ tree itself is tracked
# and must stay pristine: it is what the port is measured against.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.hypothesis/
.venv/
# frozen upstream snapshot kept only for diffing; never committed
.agents/slop/opstree/
# pin/head/work/cur checkouts an agent makes to diff both ends of a rebase.
# 191MB, and its autogen/nv_*.py are >1MiB each, so jj refuses to snapshot
# them and warns on EVERY push. Untracked is not enough: one careless
# `jj split` would sweep 191MB of another agent's scratch into a commit.
.agents/slop/xd1/

# agent scratch: in-place mutation backups and rejected merges. Committed twice
# by accident today; a .bak is a copy of a file already in the tree.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# in-place mutation scratch. Four COMPLETED PORTS were nearly lost because 5,336 uncommitted
# files made real work invisible in `jj status`. These are never sources.
*.mut.bend
_mut_*.bend
*mut.bend
probe-*.bend
probe-*.bend.mut
# Two scratch names the four lines above MISS, found by asking the question the
# patterns imply instead of the question they were written for: "does any `.bend`
# in the tree still look like scratch?". `probe-*.bend` needs the hyphen, so
# `renderer/csprobe.bend` (774 lines, a stale prefix of `cstyle.bend` -- measured
# identical for its first 588 lines) slipped through; `_mut_*.bend` needs the
# word, so `runtime/_p6.bend` (a 4-line F32.bits print) slipped through.
# `*probe.bend` matches exactly 1 file in the tree and `_*[0-9].bend` exactly 2,
# all three scratch, so neither pattern can eat a real port.
#
# BOTH ARE ALREADY TRACKED, AND A PATTERN WILL NOT UNTRACK THEM: `csprobe.bend`
# and `_p6.bend` need `rm`, then the deletion committed. Do not read a green
# `git status` here as fixed -- the same no-op is recorded twice above.
*probe.bend
_*[0-9].bend

# ops501-atrest.sh stages a REVISION of ops.bend at its own relative path, because
# a copy elsewhere cannot resolve `./../helpers.bend` and prints a phantom 0 rows.
# So the stage is necessarily inside the source tree, and two traps follow from
# that: a `for f in tinybendygrad/uop/*.bend` sweep counts it as a port and calls
# it RED when the RED is the OLD revision (observed: `ops-ATREST-20808.bend` in a
# 12-file `--check-only` sweep), and one careless `jj split` commits a whole stale
# ops.bend. Matches 0 real files.
tinybendygrad/**/*ATREST-*.bend

# comment-realignment pass: the measurement + edit harness (spec*.py, apply.py,
# final.py, cite.py, dist.py) and the four report artifacts. Never sources; the
# 2.0 MB before/ snapshot it produced was deleted so this stays under 0.5 MB.
# `.agents/slop/commentpass/README.md` says how to regenerate the snapshot.
.agents/slop/commentpass/

# browser/profile probes: an agent hunting for a WebGPU-capable browser drops a whole
# Chrome profile here (35MB .tflite models, 22MB crx blobs). Never source, never a gate input.
.agents/slop/probe/

# MNIST net.json is 2.2MB of downloaded dataset. A page fetches it; a repo does not
# carry it, and jj refuses to snapshot the whole fileset over one file.
examples/webgpu/mnist/net.json
examples/webgpu/mnist/*.gz
.agents/slop/mirror/

# Per-unit probe/working trees. An ORACLE (.py that calls CPython) and a GATE (.py/.sh that runs
# it) are the deliverable and live at slop/ TOP LEVEL; the tree a unit probed inside is not.
# NOTE: .gitignore cannot untrack a file that is already tracked -- these had to be DELETED, not
# just ignored, and the failure mode looks exactly like success.
.agents/slop/elf/
.agents/slop/elfprobe/
.agents/slop/agprobe/
.agents/slop/li/
.agents/slop/ptxown/
.agents/slop/spec/
.agents/slop/srch/
.agents/slop/ddcheck/
.agents/slop/mirror/

# .ddmut is a broken mutant from a mutation run, same class as _mut_*.bend and
# *.mut. A deliberate break in the source tree is a trap for the next reader.
tinybendygrad/**/*.ddmut

# probe-nat.bend and test/_probe/ are scratch: a hand-made probe that does not even parse
# ("expected : a term / observed : end of input"). A broken probe in the source tree is a trap
# for the next reader, not a fixture.
tinybendygrad/uop/probe-*.bend
tinybendygrad/test/_probe/
.agents/slop/dd-mirror/
.agents/slop/tv-scratch/

# Measurement caches under .agents/slop. Both were COMMITTED and both had to be DELETED,
# because .gitignore cannot untrack a file that is already tracked: a prior attempt to
# untrack net.json silently no-opped four commits, and the failure mode looks exactly like
# success. If one of these reappears, delete it -- do not treat this pattern as the fix.
#
#   ga_cache/   ga_sweep.py's output. 343 tracked files / 2.00 MB of tracked bytes
#               (25 MB on disk with the .bin lanes), written as <port>/{lane.txt,lane.rc,
#               lane.err} + lanes.json so a parser can be MEASURED offline instead of
#               re-running bend per candidate. Header says "Run once". Regenerate with
#               `python3 .agents/slop/ga_sweep.py`. NOTE ga_rows_blast.py reads it offline
#               and will not run until the sweep is re-run.
#   tv-scratch/ tree-verdict.py / state-audit.py's flat-tree working scratch, rebuilt on
#               every run. 318 tracked files / 0.55 MB. Already ignored above by name; kept
#               here so the two live together with the reason.
.agents/slop/ga_cache/
.agents/slop/*_cache/

# dd-cone-wt/ is the same class -- a per-unit probe/working tree of full littlebendygrad
# copies, 1684 tracked files -- but NOT deleted: a live agent is mid-flight in it and
# deleting it would destroy their work. Ignored so that one careless `jj split` cannot
# sweep it into a commit, for the same reason xd1/ is listed above.
.agents/slop/dd-cone-wt/

# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED. A cache-shaped path is not the test; "a report cites it" is.
# These are tracked on purpose and a future sweep must leave them alone:
#   arange-ucache/  TOOLS.md's ledger and notes/bend2-constraints.md cite it as the
#                   measurement behind the ARange ucache collision.
#   runs/           pre-split oracle baselines, tabulated in runs/README.md; the
#                   *-gate.sh scripts diff against those exact bytes.
#   probe/, commentpass/  hold AUTHORED harnesses (.py) that re-running cannot recreate.

# GENERATED OUTPUT IS NOT A SOURCE FILE. `gates/retention-check.py` CLAUSE III: "an output directory is
# not in the index" -- and it was RED with 219 entries. THE INSTRUMENT COULD NOT FIX IT BECAUSE
# `.gitignore` CANNOT UNTRECK; ONLY A COMMIT CAN, WHICH IS WHY restorekit REPORTED IT AS
# "UNSATISFIABLE-BY-ITSELF". THIS IS THAT COMMIT. THE BYTES STAY ON DISK AND IN HISTORY.
#
# A TRACKED ARTIFACT IS A FILE WHOSE VALUE LIES IN BEING REGENERABLE, AND TRACKING IT GUARANTEES THE NEXT
# GATE RUN SHOWS A DIFF THAT IS NOT A CHANGE.
gates/artifacts/
runs/
